<h2>Austin Stone-Coated Steel Repair</h2>
<p>Stone-coated steel is durable, but it is not maintenance-free, and many general roofers are unfamiliar with it. Austin Roofing provides stone-coated steel repair for homes across the metro. The problems we see most often include:</p>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Damaged panels from foot traffic.</strong> Walking on panels in the wrong spot — by satellite installers or other trades — can crush the profile and crack the coating.</li>
  <li><strong>Granule loss.</strong> Exposed steel needs to be resealed and recoated before it starts to corrode.</li>
  <li><strong>Wind-lifted or loose panels.</strong> Panels that have worked loose are re-secured and fastened to the manufacturer’s pattern.</li>
  <li><strong>Hail dents.</strong> Dented panels are documented for your insurer and replaced individually where possible.</li>
  <li><strong>Flashing and penetration leaks.</strong> Chimneys, skylights and pipe penetrations are the most common leak points on any metal roof.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where possible, we replace individual panels with matching profiles and colors rather than re-roofing whole slopes. If your roof is an older or discontinued product, we will show you the closest available match before work begins.</p>

<h2>Metal Roofing Built for Central Texas</h2>
<p>Austin metal roofing has to cope with big temperature swings. A metal panel can heat far above the air temperature in direct summer sun, then cool quickly in an evening thunderstorm. That constant expansion and contraction is why we use clip systems on standing seam, allow movement at ridges and transitions, and choose fasteners and sealants rated for the heat.</p>
<p>Metal is especially popular on rural and acreage properties in <a href="/service-areas/dripping-springs-tx/">Dripping Springs</a>, <a href="/service-areas/bastrop-tx/">Bastrop</a> and Lockhart, where wind exposure, wildfire concerns and long outbuildings make it a natural fit, as well as on modern homes in central Austin. And the old worry about rain noise? Over a solid deck with underlayment and an insulated attic, a metal roof is typically not much louder than shingles.</p>

<h2>Keeping a Metal Roof Performing for Decades</h2>
<p>Metal is low-maintenance, not no-maintenance. A few simple habits protect the investment and keep small issues from turning into leaks:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Check exposed fasteners periodically.</strong> On screw-down panels, backed-out screws and cracked washers are the number-one leak source. We replace them with oversized or new fasteners as needed.</li>
  <li><strong>Keep debris off the panels.</strong> Wet leaves and cedar litter held against metal can wear the finish and promote corrosion, especially along valleys and behind chimneys.</li>
  <li><strong>Avoid dissimilar metals.</strong> Copper and some treated lumber in contact with steel panels can cause corrosion. We use compatible flashings and fasteners.</li>
  <li><strong>Inspect sealants at penetrations.</strong> Pipe boots and sealant beads around vents and skylights age faster in the sun than the panels themselves.</li>
  <li><strong>Look after a storm.</strong> Even when dents are cosmetic, a hailstorm or high winds can loosen trim or damage flashing.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our free <a href="/services/roof-inspection/">roof inspection</a> covers all of this, with photos, so you know exactly where your metal roof stands.</p>

<h2>How a Metal Roof Installation Works</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><h3>Inspection and profile selection</h3><p>We assess the deck, pitch and structure, then walk you through profiles, gauges and colors with samples.</p></li>
  <li><h3>Measurement and ordering</h3><p>Panels are often cut to length for each slope, so accurate measurements matter more than with shingles.</p></li>
  <li><h3>Tear-off and underlayment</h3><p>The old roof is removed and the deck repaired, then a high-temperature underlayment rated for metal goes down.</p></li>
  <li><h3>Panels, trim and flashing</h3><p>Panels, clips, ridge, eave and rake trim and custom flashing are installed to the manufacturer’s details.</p></li>
  <li><h3>Cleanup and walk-through</h3><p>Metal shavings and fasteners are swept with magnets, and we review the finished roof with you.</p></li>
</ol>
